vscode: click each Problem, fix, Replace All for the logs and hope
vimrc: set errorformat=%f(%l\\,%c):\ %m hidden
open: tsc-output.txt

@brief
A ticket, not an exercise.

    ORD-560  Order.total was renamed Order.amount in the entity and the
             migration, and nothing else was. CI is red; the tsc output
             is in tsc-output.txt. Make it green. The GraphQL field is
             still called total, because the API contract does not
             change. The database column is still called total, so
             record.total stays. And while the order provider is open,
             the console.log lines that went in during the incident
             come out.

Six errors, one for every place the old name is still read as a
property of `Order`. Every one of them is fixed by turning that one
word into `amount`, and nothing else on those lines changes: `total:`
stays as an object key where it names the API field, `record.total`
stays as the column. The tsc column points at the word that is wrong,
never at the ones that are right.

Which tool is a decision. `:cdo s/total/amount/g` would be fast and
wrong: it would rename the column and the API field on the same lines.
`:g` works inside one file and these errors are in four. What fits is
the walk: the compiler put the cursor on the word, `ciw` changes it,
and chapter 11's `.` repeats that change at the next stop. The logs
are the opposite shape, several lines in one file with nothing to
decide, which is what `:g` is for.

@keys
| `:cfile` `:cn` | load the errors, step through them |
| `ciw` then `.` | change the word here, repeat it at the next stop |
| `:g/pattern/d` | delete every matching line in this file |

@hints
`:cfile tsc-output.txt`. First stop is the test factory call:
`ciw amount`, `:w`, `:cn`.
--
From the second stop on, every fix is `.`. The three in the provider
are consecutive; do the `:g/console\.log/d` while you are in that file
and the remaining entries in it still land where they should.
--
`:w` before each `:cn`, or `hidden` is on and `:wqa` at the end covers
it. Six errors, six stops, `:wq` after the last.
--
Par assumes `ciw` once and `.` five times, one `:g`, and a `:w` per
file. Nothing here needs a visual selection or a register.

@solution
    :cfile tsc-output.txt<Enter>  ciw amount <Esc> :w<Enter>
    :cn<Enter> .  :cn<Enter> .  :cn<Enter> .  :g/console\.log/d<Enter> :w<Enter>
    :cn<Enter> . :w<Enter>  :cn<Enter> . :wq<Enter>

Three tools were on the table and the ticket needed two of them. The
question that picks between them is not "how many hits" but "how many
decisions per hit". Zero decisions across many files: `:cdo`. Zero
decisions inside one file: `:g` or `:%s`. One decision per hit, with
the edit the same each time: the list plus `.`, which is what this
was. One decision per hit with a different edit each time: the list on
its own, as in lesson 3. Chapter 21 adds a macro to that ladder, for
when the edit is the same but too long for `.` to hold.

The `:g` in the middle of a walk was safe for the reason lesson 11
gave: the remaining entries in that buffer moved with the lines. And
the tsc columns were exact enough that no fix needed a motion first,
which is the compiler doing the navigation and you doing only the
edit. That division of labour is what the whole chapter was building
toward: a list of places from a search, a grep, or a build, and your
hands free for the part that needs a person.

@start README.md
# Orders service

Cancelling an order refunds it through `PaymentService.sendRefund`, which
is named after the gateway's `/sendRefund` endpoint. A refund the gateway
rejects raises `REFUND_FAILED`. Refund events go out on the
`payment.sendRefund` routing key, which the ledger service consumes.

@start src/domain/order/order.entity.ts
export type Order = {
  id: string;
  customerId: string;
  status: OrderStatus;
  amount: number;
  placedAt: Date;
};

export type OrderStatus = 'PENDING' | 'SHIPPED' | 'CANCELLED';

@start src/domain/order/order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { formatMoney } from '../../shared/money';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    console.log('cancel', id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    if (order.total > 0) {
      console.log('refunding', order.total);
      await this.paymentService.issueRefund(order.id);
    }

    console.log('cancelled', id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }

  public async summary(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    return { id: order.id, total: formatMoney(order.total) };
  }
}

@expected src/domain/order/order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { formatMoney } from '../../shared/money';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);


    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    if (order.amount > 0) {
      await this.paymentService.issueRefund(order.id);
    }


    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }

  public async summary(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    return { id: order.id, total: formatMoney(order.amount) };
  }
}

@start src/domain/order/order.provider.test.ts
import { stub, reveal } from 'jest-auto-stub';
import { OrderProvider } from './order.provider';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { orderFactory } from '../../../test/factories/order.factory';

describe('OrderProvider', () => {
  const orderRepository = stub<OrderRepository>();
  const paymentService = stub<PaymentService>();
  const provider = new OrderProvider(orderRepository, paymentService);

  afterEach(() => jest.resetAllMocks());

  it('refunds a pending order when it is cancelled', async () => {
    const order = orderFactory({ status: 'PENDING', total: 250 });
    reveal(orderRepository).findOne.mockResolvedValue(order);
    reveal(paymentService).issueRefund.mockResolvedValue(undefined);

    await provider.cancel(order.id);

    expect(paymentService.issueRefund).toHaveBeenCalledWith(order.id);
  });

  it('refuses to cancel a shipped order', async () => {
    const order = orderFactory({ status: 'SHIPPED' });
    reveal(orderRepository).findOne.mockResolvedValue(order);

    await expect(provider.cancel(order.id)).rejects.toThrow('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    expect(paymentService.issueRefund).not.toHaveBeenCalled();
  });
});

@expected src/domain/order/order.provider.test.ts
import { stub, reveal } from 'jest-auto-stub';
import { OrderProvider } from './order.provider';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { orderFactory } from '../../../test/factories/order.factory';

describe('OrderProvider', () => {
  const orderRepository = stub<OrderRepository>();
  const paymentService = stub<PaymentService>();
  const provider = new OrderProvider(orderRepository, paymentService);

  afterEach(() => jest.resetAllMocks());

  it('refunds a pending order when it is cancelled', async () => {
    const order = orderFactory({ status: 'PENDING', amount: 250 });
    reveal(orderRepository).findOne.mockResolvedValue(order);
    reveal(paymentService).issueRefund.mockResolvedValue(undefined);

    await provider.cancel(order.id);

    expect(paymentService.issueRefund).toHaveBeenCalledWith(order.id);
  });

  it('refuses to cancel a shipped order', async () => {
    const order = orderFactory({ status: 'SHIPPED' });
    reveal(orderRepository).findOne.mockResolvedValue(order);

    await expect(provider.cancel(order.id)).rejects.toThrow('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    expect(paymentService.issueRefund).not.toHaveBeenCalled();
  });
});

@start src/domain/order/order.repository.ts
import { injectable } from 'tsyringe';
import { Order as OrderRecord } from '@prisma/client';
import { BaseRepository } from '../../infrastructure/base.repository';
import { Order } from './order.entity';

@injectable()
export class OrderRepository extends BaseRepository<OrderRecord, Order> {
  public async findByCustomer(args: { customerId: string }) {
    const records = await this.prisma.order.findMany({
      where: { customerId: args.customerId, deleted: null },
    });

    return records.map((record) => this.toEntity(record));
  }

  public toEntity(record: OrderRecord): Order {
    return {
      id: record.id,
      customerId: record.customerId,
      status: record.status,
      total: record.total,
      placedAt: record.placedAt,
    };
  }
}

@expected src/domain/order/order.repository.ts
import { injectable } from 'tsyringe';
import { Order as OrderRecord } from '@prisma/client';
import { BaseRepository } from '../../infrastructure/base.repository';
import { Order } from './order.entity';

@injectable()
export class OrderRepository extends BaseRepository<OrderRecord, Order> {
  public async findByCustomer(args: { customerId: string }) {
    const records = await this.prisma.order.findMany({
      where: { customerId: args.customerId, deleted: null },
    });

    return records.map((record) => this.toEntity(record));
  }

  public toEntity(record: OrderRecord): Order {
    return {
      id: record.id,
      customerId: record.customerId,
      status: record.status,
      amount: record.total,
      placedAt: record.placedAt,
    };
  }
}

@start src/domain/order/order.resolver.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { OrderProvider } from './order.provider';

@injectable()
export class OrderResolver {
  constructor(@inject(OrderProvider) protected orderProvider: OrderProvider) {}

  public async order(_: unknown, args: { id: string }) {
    return this.orderProvider.findOne(args.id);
  }

  public async cancelOrder(_: unknown, args: { id: string }) {
    return this.orderProvider.cancel(args.id);
  }

  public async orderSummary(_: unknown, args: { id: string }) {
    const order = await this.orderProvider.findOne(args.id);

    return { id: order.id, status: order.status, total: order.total };
  }
}

@expected src/domain/order/order.resolver.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { OrderProvider } from './order.provider';

@injectable()
export class OrderResolver {
  constructor(@inject(OrderProvider) protected orderProvider: OrderProvider) {}

  public async order(_: unknown, args: { id: string }) {
    return this.orderProvider.findOne(args.id);
  }

  public async cancelOrder(_: unknown, args: { id: string }) {
    return this.orderProvider.cancel(args.id);
  }

  public async orderSummary(_: unknown, args: { id: string }) {
    const order = await this.orderProvider.findOne(args.id);

    return { id: order.id, status: order.status, total: order.amount };
  }
}

